A||||2||CanadianGT||Some guy wanted to race....in a Fiero!||||1||
Z||000000||CanadianGT||08-21-2001||05:49 PM||||Well I am at these stop lights, and at the lights to my right is a White fastback GT.  I tried to get his attention, but to no avail.  So I turn onto a two lane road and when I look in my rear view, there it is taking a corner fast trying to catch up to me, as I guess he see's me afterall!  So he finally does catch me at the next lights, and pulls into the lane right next to me, but looks straight ahead.  I look over at him, and he finally looks over at me with this big smile!!  I said "nice ride".  Then the light turns green, and I thought about gunning it, but decided against it since my rebuild was only about 300 KM ago.  I slowly pulled ahead of him, then all of a sudden I hear this huge sounding engine rev, and he blows by me by 3 or 4 car lengths then hits the breaks. His front end kind of went up.  When I am side by side with him again , we both smiled at eachother, then I had to turn off at my street. Even though we did not race eachother for real, it was so awesome being at a stop light right next to another Fiero GT, with the  "chance", to race.  Had my engine been broken in, I would have done it!!  It was also cool, since when the light was red, I was looking at the faces of the people behind us at the light in both lanes, and they were pointing at both are cars, and it looked like they all wanted to see a race!!<BR>Anyways, just had to share the experience, as normally it is only Hopped up civic punks that want to go, not Fiero's!!! Anyone else have a race against a fiero??<BR>PeAcE<BR>Kyle<BR>P.S. ( How long until an engine is properly broken in, and what steps should I follow?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||baldlobo||08-21-2001||08:12 PM||||nice, I think 5,000km is a good break in period.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever3000||08-21-2001||08:16 PM||||Long time ago I was told 500 miles of gentle driving, then change the oil & filter, and that's it.<BR>||||reg||1
